# ==============================================================================
# .gitignore for Academic Claude Code Projects
# ==============================================================================

# LaTeX build artifacts
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.log
*.nav
*.out
*.snm
*.toc
*.vrb
*.synctex.gz
*.run.xml
*-blx.bib

# Compiled PDFs (uncomment to track specific PDFs)
# *.pdf

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# R
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rdata

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local secrets / scratch (never commit)
.env
_cv.txt

# Assignment solution keys — never commit or publish. Keeps the public
# GitHub Pages site (docs/) and the source tree (Assignments/) free of
# answer keys; sync_to_docs.sh excludes them too.
**/*-solutions.tex
**/*-solutions.pdf
Assignments/CS401/*-solutions.*

# Minor exam papers — internal institutional sessional exams. Unlike
# Assignments/CompetitiveExam (whose student-facing questions ARE public
# study material and only the solution keys are gitignored), a Minor paper
# is a real, live exam given to real students — the question paper itself
# must never leak via this public GitHub repo. Both the paper and its
# solution key are gitignored wholesale, never committed, never synced to
# docs/. See .claude/skills/create-minor-paper/SKILL.md.
Minors/**

# Coding-assignment instructor-only files — reference solutions, hidden test
# suites, and autograder harnesses must never reach the public repo or the
# GitHub Pages site. The student-facing pieces (bag.h, starter_*.c,
# test_visible.c, and the problem-statement PDF) remain tracked.
Assignments/**/*-coding/reference_*

# Grading data — real student submissions, draft grading reports, approved
# score ledgers, and computed attainment numbers all carry PII. Never commit
# or publish (same posture as the solution keys above). See
# .claude/rules/grading-protocol.md for the full contract.
Submissions/
quality_reports/grading/
Assignments/**/*-scores-approved.yaml
Accreditation/**/attainment-data.yaml
Assignments/**/*-coding/test_hidden.*
Assignments/**/*-coding/autograder.*

# Claude Code local files (not shared across machines)
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/state/
CLAUDE.local.md

# IDE
# .vscode/settings.json ships in the template (carries shipped Claude Code permission-mode
# recommendations — see TROUBLESHOOTING.md "Permissions / bypass / statusline" for the typo
# fix forkers need). Other .vscode/ content is developer-machine-specific.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Quarto rendering artifacts
.quarto/
# In-place renders next to the .qmd source. Only the .qmd (and theme .scss) are
# tracked under Quarto/ — the published HTML lives in docs/, put there by
# scripts/sync_to_docs.sh. A stray render beside the source is a build artifact.
Quarto/**/*.html
Quarto/**/*_files/

# quality_reports/ — per-project session logs, plans, specs, merges, audits,
# diagnoses. The directory structure ships in the template (via .gitkeep), but
# the content is PROJECT-INTERNAL and shouldn't be inherited by forks.
# (diagnoses/ in particular may hold real data values/paths — never ship them;
#  audits/ are repo-specific gap analyses, noise for a forker.)
quality_reports/plans/*
quality_reports/specs/*
quality_reports/session_logs/*
quality_reports/merges/*
quality_reports/decisions/*
quality_reports/checkpoints/*
quality_reports/preregistrations/*
quality_reports/audits/*
quality_reports/diagnoses/*
!quality_reports/plans/.gitkeep
!quality_reports/specs/.gitkeep
!quality_reports/session_logs/.gitkeep
!quality_reports/merges/.gitkeep
!quality_reports/decisions/.gitkeep
!quality_reports/checkpoints/.gitkeep
!quality_reports/preregistrations/.gitkeep
!quality_reports/audits/.gitkeep
!quality_reports/diagnoses/.gitkeep

# R analysis outputs (generated artifacts; keep scripts, ignore outputs)
scripts/R/_outputs/

# Playwright scratch workspace (verification scripts, screenshots, node_modules)
reference/

# Textbook source material — copyrighted scans/PDFs and raw full-text
# extraction dumps must never be committed. Only the derived index.md
# (chapters/pages/key-terms, no substantial verbatim text) is tracked.
master_supporting_docs/**/supporting_books/**/*.pdf
master_supporting_docs/**/supporting_books/**/*_fulltext.txt
master_supporting_docs/**/supporting_books/**/extracted/

# MSYS crash dumps (Windows) — never commit
**/bash.exe.stackdump
bash.exe.stackdump

# Department timetables — contain other branches' schedules and other
# faculty members' names/room assignments, not just this instructor's own
# courses. Kept local-only; never published (this repo and docs/ are both
# public). Only the CS401 class-day pattern derived from them is committed,
# via docs/calendar/ics/cs401.ics.
Timetable/

# Output artifacts — uncomment lines below based on your preference
# *.rds
# output/**/*.rds
